## Say what broke

`SuperRatifyBridge.Model.forked` needed repair — and the reason is a STRENGTHENING: its hidden fork hung
off a non-participant genesis, so under the filtered clock it collapses to the leader's round and the
node correctly refuses that wave. Signatures ripple to `StrandAdmission`, `TauPrefixMonotone`,
`SuperRatifyBridge`.

## Two findings from driving it

⚑ **A FOURTH FORK MECHANISM, measured not inferred**: after the fix the two views still differ
intra-cohort, because `poll_finalized_blocks` **re-hashes each block over only the acks that resolved**,
so the ordering-lace id — `xsort`'s tie-break — is a function of the VIEW. Reproduced
(`ordering_projection_ids`); the fix is in `node/src/blocklace_sync.rs`, left to its owner.

**The upstream gate, checked rather than assumed**: the two-honest-view fork is NOT reachable via gossip
(`insert_checked`/`merge` enforce closure). It is reachable via `from_checkpoint_trusted`, which has no
closure check. **The stall needs no divergence at all.**

